# Commit Messages

Only create a commit when the user explicitly asks. Follow Conventional Commits
in English (match existing history).

## Format

```
type(scope): imperative summary

Optional body explaining why, not a file list.
```

- Subject: ≤72 chars, imperative mood, no trailing period
- Body: wrap ~72 chars; focus on **why**, not what changed file-by-file
- Pass the message via HEREDOC (`git commit -m "$(cat <<'EOF' ... EOF)"`)

## Types

| type | use when |
|------|----------|
| `feat` | new user-facing capability |
| `fix` | bug fix |
| `refactor` | internal change, same behavior |
| `perf` | performance improvement |
| `style` | formatting / visual-only (no logic) |
| `chore` | tooling, config, deps, ignore files |
| `docs` | documentation only |
| `build` | build / bundler / CI scripts |

## Scopes (prefer these)

`web` · `forms` · `api` · `ui` · `i18n` · `config` · `deps`

Omit scope only when the change is truly cross-cutting.

## Ticket references

If a Linear/issue id is known (e.g. `CYN-11`), append it in the subject or body:
`feat(forms): add device preview lab (CYN-11)`.

## Examples

```
feat(forms): add calculated-field empty state until sources exist

fix(api): surface structured errors from AI chat stream

refactor(ui): colocate device frame chrome with preview lab

chore(config): tighten ignore patterns for generated route tree
```

## Anti-patterns

```
# ❌ vague / file dump
update stuff
fix bugs
feat: update FormDesignerLayout.tsx and i18n files

# ❌ past tense / trailing period
Fixed the autosave race.
```
